Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: klipr
Upstream-Contact: Nguyen Duc <nguyenminhduc230903@gmail.com>
Source: https://github.com/NguyenDuc2309/klipr
Comment:
 The upstream git tree carries the project's marketing website under landing/,
 which is no part of the packaged program: nothing in it is built, installed or
 run by this package. It also embeds a self-hosted APT repository holding
 prebuilt binaries (a .deb pool, a dearmoured keyring and signed index files),
 which must not appear in a Debian source package at all. The whole directory
 is dropped, along with byte-compiled Python caches and stray build output;
 this is why the upstream version carries a +ds suffix.
Files-Excluded:
 landing
 */__pycache__
 *.pyc
 klipr_*.deb

